# Out-of-range TRUNC/ROUND arguments for tests/contract/trunc_round_range.sh:
# call|exact stderr. The suite puts the call into trunc_round_invalid.pas and
# prepends {$MATHCK+} or {$MATHCK-} (the range check is independent of
# MATHCK), so the call is at line 7 column 8. r and z are 0.0; z / z is NaN.
# Results outside -32768..32767 fail (IBM 11-6, "ABS(X) > MAXINT"); ROUND
# rounds half away from zero, so +-0.5 beyond the limits is already out of
# range. The diagnostic reports the REAL argument value.
TRUNC(r + 32768.0)|runtime error: TRUNC result out of INTEGER range at line 7 column 8 (value=32768)
TRUNC(r - 32769.0)|runtime error: TRUNC result out of INTEGER range at line 7 column 8 (value=-32769)
TRUNC(r + 1.0E300)|runtime error: TRUNC result out of INTEGER range at line 7 column 8 (value=1.0000000000000001e+300)
TRUNC(z / z)|runtime error: TRUNC result out of INTEGER range at line 7 column 8 (value=NaN)
ROUND(r + 32767.5)|runtime error: ROUND result out of INTEGER range at line 7 column 8 (value=32767.5)
ROUND(r - 32768.5)|runtime error: ROUND result out of INTEGER range at line 7 column 8 (value=-32768.5)
ROUND(r - 1.0E300)|runtime error: ROUND result out of INTEGER range at line 7 column 8 (value=-1.0000000000000001e+300)
ROUND(z / z)|runtime error: ROUND result out of INTEGER range at line 7 column 8 (value=NaN)
